<title>UK: RheinHyp plans 1.0 bln mark seven-year Pfandbrief.</title>
<headline>RheinHyp plans 1.0 bln mark seven-year Pfandbrief.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rheinische Hypothekenbank plans to launch a 1.0 billion mark seven-year Pfandbrief, joint lead manager ABN AMRO Hoare Govett said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The other joint lead managers are BZW, CDC Marche, Dresdner Kleinwort Benson and HSBC Trinkaus.</p>
<p>The deal, expected to be launched on Thursday, subject to market conditions, will will be priced around one basis point over the 6.75 percent Bund due July 15, 2004. The coupon is expected to be 4.75 percent.</p>
<p>--Denise Manning, London newsroom,  +44 171 542 7658</p>
